// Justification letters (you must use one)
//	l = left
//	c = center

{1000}{171c





Technology and the Future

Written by:
Victor Von Doom}

{1001}{171l








There is a storm on the horizon.  It will arrive in the blink of an eye with all the sound and the fury of a raging tempest.  That storm is our technilogical revolution and it is the final nail in the coffin of a dying religion, that of magic.  The mage relies on his willpower to bend the laws that govern who we are.  The very thought is an abomination to existence, and all who practice this witchcraft must be dealt with swiftly and definitively.  The mage cannot be tolerated in modern society especially since his existence threatens the well being of us all.  The more this foul discipline is practiced the greater the threat to the stability of our very world!  It has been shown that the use of magic tears at the fabric of our reality, thus weakening it.  How much longer before it finally tears apart?  Fear not though.  We can overcome this - we shall overcome this, with the complete and utter annihilation of all magic users in Arcanum.}



{1010}{497c





The Great Battle Between Victor Von Doom and The Evil Dragon Fin Fang Foom

Written by:
Baron Von Zemo}

{1011}{497l




There is little that isn't owed to our great and fearless savior Victor Von Doom.  He single-handedly delivered the death blow that ended the threat of Fin Fang Foom forever.  Lord Doom traveled with a party of his finest men to the ruins in the northwest.  The ruins which housed the slumbering Fin Fang Foom.  This dragon had terrorized the lands of Arcanum in previous centuries and legend told of its hibernation and - more importantly - it spoke of its reawakening.  Lord Doom decided to end the threat before it could arise again.  The road was hard and he lost a few men just traveling from Latveria to the ruins.  Once there they entered the ruins and had to contend with all manner of foul and magical beasts.  The fact that they were able to navigate their way through the dark and perilous dungeons while facing a horde of these creatures is testament enough to Lord Doom's greatness.  However even after making their way through this nightmare, they had to contend with Fin Fang Foom himself.  Lord Doom lost many good men that day, and only after hours of torturous battle was he able to finally deal the killing blow to the beast and bring peace and harmony to our lands.}



{1020}{28c
Technology is the sweet fragrance of the land, granted by those on high - the mighty and powerful Technology Gods.  Verily it is because of their divine power and grace that we can enjoy the fruits of technology and can use this technology to the glory and the honor of our Technology Gods.  Praise be to the Technology Gods and may they bestow their technological blessings upon us for all time.  Amen.}



{1030}{37c







The History of Latveria

Written by:
Otto Octavius}

{1031}{37l









Latveria is the jewel at the heart of Arcanum.  Founded in 1810 by the much respected and revered Sir Werner Von Doom, Latveria has been a mecca of technological advancement and superiority.  Even the largest city in Arcanum, Tarant, recognizes Latveria's place in the history of technology throughout the century.  From Sir Victor Von Doom's improvements concerning the capabilities of firearms, to Tony Stark's superior armour construction, Latveria continues to push the limits of technology.}



{1040}{28c







Prophecy of the Nameless One}

{1041}{28l








[this book is in bad shape and there are only a few passages that are legible]

...and it shall come to pass that the nameless one shall return.  But he comes not to bring peace to the world, but a sword...


...and he shall have a herald to prepare the way.  And that herald shall be called Fin Fang Foom.  He will prepare the way for the nameless one, and his death shall trigger the events leading to the nameless one's return...


...and the nameless one shall bring a great cleansing to the land...}



{1050}{37c





Technology Compendium

Written by:
Otto Octavius}

{1051}{37l










The progress made by technology in the past century is nothing short of astounding.  From thrown rocks, to bows, to the most rudimentary of pistols, to the fantastic power of the elephant gun, the inventions of technology may very well be reaching their limit.  Most everything imaginable has already been invented!  Gilbert Bates ushered in the age of the steam engine and now most of our hard labor can be performed by machines.  Defensively, what could be better protection than covering one's entire body in iron?  Advancements are still being made in technology, but I feel confident that we will be able to close the patent office by the end of the century.}


{1060}{37c








CR Report}

{1061}{37l










Semptember 3

We've discovered pieces of material that are too small for the human eye to see.  Astounding!  By using powerful lenses with a combination of intense light, we are able to actually see this material (called 'particles' from here on).










Semptember 10

There are an amazing number of particles just about everywhere!  In many places when we focus a lens we see too many to count.  We're not sure about any of their properties yet, but we are going to keep investigating them.










October 5

Interesting.  When we destroy a single particle, nothing appears to happen - as long as there are no other particles in the vicinity.  If we destroy a particle and there are four or more in its vicinity, it creates a type of chain reaction (called CR from here on) that destroys the other nearby particles!








October 24

We believe the CR of the particles can somehow be weaponized.  It will take the exact amount of particles and something to trigger their destruction to make it work, but it is only a matter of time before we unlock the correct combination.}


{1070}{37c





Doomsday
Verson 1.1
Created By:   Quaid
Created On:   October 10, 2007
Last Update:  October 14, 2007}

{1071}{37l










First, thank you for taking the time to load this module into your computer.  I've worked long and hard to bring you a playable adventure and I hope you enjoy it.

This module takes place in Arcanum, but you cannot travel to any of the places from the original game.  It is a stand alone adventure.

In the fountain where you found this book are some goodies to get your character started.

I would like to thank Troika for making Arcanum, and Terra Arcanum: The House of Lords for all of the help I've received while building this module.  Special thanks to Dark Underlord for putting together the AMTUT tutorial, without which I wouldn't have known where to start.  And a special thanks to rroyo who made every effort to answer any questions I came up with during the building of this adventure, and helped me to playtest this adventure.

If you would like to leave comments, criticisms, or suggestions please feel free to contact me at Terra Arcanum:  The House of Lords (http://terra-arcanum.com/phpBB/) or email me at:  johnmv1@juno.com

Happy Adventuring!
-Quaid






